    "https://apply.interfolio.com/189344": {
      "title": "Term Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) - Counseling & Special Education (26-27)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF EDUCATION: COUNSELING SPECIAL ED Location: Chicago, IL - College of Education The Counseling Program at DePaul University seeks to fill one ten-month, full-time, non-tenure track faculty position in Counseling Education to teach introductory and advanced master’s-level courses in areas such counseling core, clinical mental health, and/or school counseling (six courses over the academic year). Depending upon the academic quarter, this faculty member might teach online asynchronously/synchronously as well as in person on our Lincoln Park (Chicago) campus. In addition, this non-tenure track faculty position will have three course reallocations (one-per-quarter) to coordinate and supervise counseling interns in our Education and Counseling Center (ECC) in the College of Education. Responsibilities may include the following: Recruit, interview, onboard, and complete deprovisioning process for student counselors. Track and assign new clients to student counselors. Manage the Titanium web-processing and record management system; review, approve, and audit student counselor notes providing feedback. Provide orientation and training to new student counselors. Establish and maintain partnerships with internal and external collaborators to ensure consistent referral stream; collaborate with FCS director to facilitate space sharing. Provide weekly supervision for student counselors. Establish initiatives for expanding ECC scope to provide services to external community members. Finally, this non-tenure track position provides support for departmental and programmatic initiatives that seek to create a culture of student engagement, critical inquiry, and the development of counselors as practitioners, scholars, and leaders. Availability for on-campus meetings is expected. Minimum qualifications include an earned doctorate in Counseling or Counselor Education, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Active participation in counseling education professional associations is preferred. Applications must be submitted by no later than the deadline, however, confidential letters of recommendation can still be uploaded by the recommender after the deadline. Keep in mind though that an interview cannot be conducted until all letters have been received and reviewed by the search committee. Confidential letters must be uploaded through the system by the recommender, please do not email letters of recommendation to the college. Feel free reach out to Erin James at ejames17@depaul.edu if you have any additional questions. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx. About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192189": {
      "title": "Term Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) - AUSL Lincoln Park Campus (26-27)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF EDUCATION: COUNSELING SPECIAL ED Location: Chicago, IL - College of Education The Special Education and Reading program at DePaul University seeks to fill a full time, non-tenure track faculty position in Special Education to teach in undergraduate and masters level special education programs. The appointment will begin December 1, 2026 and go through June 30, 2027. Applications will be accepted immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and masters level special education courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online formats, possibly including courses at the University Center in Lake County. Additional responsibilities include faculty advising, contributing to initiatives to enhance special education programs and active participation in College, Department, and Special Education Program meetings. We seek an individual who shares our vision of becoming the preferred provider of special education programming in the Chicago area. Required Qualifications: A doctorate in Special Education or a closely related field, however candidates with a masters degree in Special Education and extensive teaching experience will also be considered. Expertise in theory and practice related to teaching reading or mathematics to exceptional learners. Expertise in instruction and differentiation in special education, assessment, and assistive technology. Preferred qualifications include prior experience with: applied practice in K-12 settings. university level teaching. online or hybrid teaching in higher education. practicum or student teaching supervision. Please keep in mind that interviews cannot be conducted until all confidential letter of recommendation have been received and reviewed by the search committee. Confidential letters must be uploaded through the system by the recommender, please do not email letters of recommendation to the college. Feel free reach out to Erin James at ejames17@depaul.edu if you have any additional questions regarding the position or application process. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188838": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Cybersecurity (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: CDM: SCHOOL OF COMPUTING Location: Chicago, IL - Jarvis College of Computing & Digital Media The School of Computing at DePaul University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position. We are particularly seeking candidates with expertise in Cybersecurity . The School of Computing houses a robust Cybersecurity Center with state-of-the-art facilities including a newly developed Cybersecurity Lab featuring dedicated server infrastructure for advanced security and privacy research, multi-user attack/defense hands-on experimentation, and extensive AI/ML integration for studying emerging cybersecurity threats. Our cybersecurity program is supported by specialized research labs including the Secure Design Lab and the Actionable Cybersecurity & Accessibility Lab (ACAL), focused on exploring, designing, and developing human-centered, accessible solutions driven towards resilience against any form of deception in cyberspace. The School of Computing includes over 70 full-time faculty and more than 3,600 undergraduate and graduate students. We offer a PhD program, 17 master's degrees, and 10 bachelor’s degrees as well as a growing number multidisciplinary CS plus X degrees. The School of Computing is committed to providing a flexible and supportive environment for its faculty, promoting a rewarding academic career with a balance between teaching and research. Located in the heart of Chicago’s vibrant downtown, it offers vast opportunities to forge relationships industry, national laboratories, universities, and other organizations in the Chicago area. The School of Computing has several centers of excellence, including Big Data, Cloud Infrastructure, and High-Performance Computing; Visual Computing, Medical Informatics, and Bioinformatics; Web Intelligence and Recommender Systems; Computing Education; Interactive Machine Learning; Cybersecurity and Adversarial Machine Learning; Computational Geometry and Topology; Next Generation Networks; Rehabilitation Robotics; and Intelligent Software Engineering. Over the past decade, faculty within the school have secured more than $15M in NSF funding and consistently published in selective conferences. The culture within the school emphasizes high-impact and high-quality research, rather than placing pressure on faculty to secure external funding or publish many papers. Nonetheless, the university provides extensive support for external funding, as well as a robust internal research grants program, including PhD stipends, graduate assistantships and course releases. Applicants should have a PhD degree in Computer Science, or a related field. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and continue until the positions are filled. The application must include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Contact information for at least three professional references - references will be contacted to upload their recommendations Research statement highlighting both current and future directions of research Teaching statement For more information, contact Filipo Sharevski ( fsharevs@depaul.edu ). General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/192343": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Editing (Tenure-Track) (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: CDM: SCHOOL OF CINEMATIC ARTS Location: Chicago, IL - Jarvis College of Computing & Digital Media The School of Cinematic Arts at DePaul University seeks an editor for a tenure-track position in one of the most innovative cinema programs in the country. The position begins in September 2027. DePaul University is located in the heart of Chicago's vibrant Loop and Lincoln Park communities. In 2026, the School of Cinematic Arts was ranked 10th in Hollywood Reporter’s annual list of the top film schools in the country and first in the Midwest. There are currently over 2,000 majors enrolled in our degree programs in Film & Television and Animation with concentrations in editing among 15 other disciplines. DePaul has advanced the field of education for editing and is expanding its curriculum, faculty, and technology to be the leadership institution for post-production training and research in the Midwest. Resources include six sound stages at Cinespace Studios, the Jarvis Center for Innovation and Collaboration, two sound studios, color and editing suites, industry-standard camera packages, a virtual production studio, motion capture systems, a television studio, and two theaters. For more information about the School of Cinematic Arts programs, please visit our website: http://www.cdm.depaul.edu/about/Pages/School-of-Cinematic-Arts.aspx Ideal candidates for the position will have extensive experience in one or more of the following areas: editing for feature films, television, or documentary. Experience with color correction, sound, or post production finishing workflows is highly desired. College-level teaching experience desired. Job responsibilities include teaching, curricular development, service, supervising student/faculty projects and continued creative activities and/or scholarship in the field. Terminal degree and/or equivalent professional experience is required. For priority consideration, apply by November 1, 2026. To apply, include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy , a URL of samples of relevant creative work and/or scholarship, and contact information for at least three professional references (references will be contacted to upload their recommendations). General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length. The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/194106": {
      "title": "Term Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) - Screenwriting (26-27)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: CDM: SCHOOL OF CINEMATIC ARTS Location: Chicago, IL - Jarvis College of Computing & Digital Media The School of Cinematic Arts (SCA) at DePaul University invites applicants for a full-time, renewable, non-tenure track Professional Lecturer position in Screenwriting – Television Writing. SCA offers Screenwriting and Showrunning concentrations to our BFA students, as well as an MFA in Screenwriting featuring standard and comedy concentrations for graduate students. DePaul University is in the heart of Chicago's vibrant Loop and Lincoln Park communities. In 2026, the SCA was ranked 10th in The Hollywood Reporter ’s annual list of the top film schools in the country. SCA currently enrolls over 2,000 students in its BA, BFA, BS, MS and MFA degree programs. Production resources include six full sound stages at Cinespace Studios, two green screen stages, a virtual production volume, studios for motion capture, television, and sound, plus industry-standard camera packages and a 4k digital cinema theatre. This position begins in March 2027. Responsibilities Job responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in writing for television, as well as committee service at the school and college level, supervising student projects, and continued professional development. Required Qualifications: Record of professional practice and/or creative activity in writing for television is required. Successful applicants will be able to teach theoretical and practical hands-on courses, will have industry and/or academic experience, and are motivated to work with faculty and students on building curriculum, leading school-wide initiatives, and/or participating on collaborative projects. Preferred Qualifications: MFA degree or equivalent industry experience in writing for television Exemplary communication and collaboration skills Post secondary teaching experience For priority consideration, apply by January 4, 2027. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Required Documents Curriculum vitae or resume Cover letter Links to creative work, including writing samples and/or produced television Contact information for three professional references (references will be contacted to upload their recommendations) General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length. The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188852": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Economics (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: DRIEHAUS COLLEGE OF BUSINESS: ECONOMICS Location: Chicago, IL - Driehaus College of Business The Department of Economics at DePaul University invites applications for two tenure-track positions at the Assistant Professor level with an expected start date of July 1, 2027.  We are looking for empirically oriented candidates in three distinct areas.  These include macroeconomics, urban economics, and business economics, which we broadly think of as the application of economics to business decision-making.  The business economics position could span a range of fields, including behavioral economics, and the right candidate will actively contribute to our MBA program. Within macroeconomics, we are particularly interested in candidates specializing in international macroeconomics, macro-finance, or macroeconomic history. We are open to a broad range of areas within urban economics. Responsibilities: - Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the candidate’s field of specialty. - Produce high-quality original research and actively contribute to the intellectual life of the department. - Participate in departmental and university service activities. Located in the center of Chicago's downtown, DePaul’s Driehaus College of Business immerses students in one of the world’s great business centers to provide transformative, hands-on educational experiences. Enrolling over 5,400 students, Driehaus’s undergraduate and graduate programs are highly ranked and nationally recognized. Founded in 1912, Driehaus was among the first 10 business colleges in the United States and the first at an American Catholic university.  The Driehaus mission is to empower students to become socially responsible leaders who make an impact in their communities. Guided by our Catholic and Vincentian values and aided by our deep roots in the City of Chicago, we deliver a cutting-edge business education, generate pathbreaking research, and collaborate closely with our community and industry partners to drive positive social outcomes. Visit https://business.depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx - Ph.D. in Economics or closely related field by the start date. - Demonstrated potential for producing significant research contributions. - Strong teaching skills and a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education. Please submit: 1. Cover Letter detailing your interest in the position. 2. Curriculum Vitae. 3. Research statement. 4. Teaching statement. 5. Three confidential reference letters. 6. Job market paper and/or other writing samples. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188853": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Management & Entrepreneurship (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: DRIEHAUS COLLEGE OF BUSINESS: MANAGEMENT & ENTREPRENEURSHIP Location: Chicago, IL - Driehaus College of Business The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship at DePaul University's Driehaus College of Business invites applications for a full-time assistant professor tenure-track position in strategic management beginning academic year 2027-2028 . Applicants must have a doctorate in strategic management or related field (ABD considered). Prior university teaching experience is preferred and candidates with industry experience are welcome. We also invite applications from candidates with experience and a track record of publication in top journals seeking credit toward tenure. Responsibilities of the position will include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in strategic management, maintaining a program of active scholarship and university service. The opening is for a faculty member who primarily specializes in strategic management. However, candidates with supplemental experience or interest in teaching or research in entrepreneurship, international business, or business and society in addition to strategic management are also welcome. We are especially interested in candidates whose work and interests align with DePaul's Vincentian mission which calls on the university to address the great questions of our day, promoting peaceful, just, and equitable solutions to social and environmental challenges. The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship houses a diverse, multi-disciplinary and research-active faculty who support undergraduate and graduate programs in business analytics, human resource management, entrepreneurship, general management, supply chain management, and sustainability management. Faculty publish in leading journals including Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Strategic Management Journal, Journal of Management, Leadership Quarterly, Journal of Business Venturing, and Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice, among others. Many of the department's faculty also support the college's rigorous Doctorate in Business Administration program. The department is also home to the Coleman Center for Entrepreneurship. A number of active student groups are affiliated with the department. Located in the center of Chicago's downtown, DePaul's Driehaus College of Business immerses students in one of the world's great business centers to provide transformative, hands-on educational experiences. Enrolling over 5,400 students, Driehaus's undergraduate and graduate programs are highly ranked and nationally recognized. Founded in 1912, Driehaus was among the first 10 business colleges in the United States and the first at an American Catholic university. The Driehaus mission is to empower students to become socially responsible leaders who make an impact in their communities. Guided by our Catholic and Vincentian values and aided by our deep roots in the City of Chicago, we deliver a cutting-edge business education, generate pathbreaking research, and collaborate closely with our community and industry partners to drive positive social outcomes. Visit https://business. depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx Applicants will be asked to submit a CV, cover letter, teaching statement, research statement, sample publications, teaching evaluations, and contact information for references. The position will remain open until filled and review of applications will begin immediately. Applications received by September 30th will receive full consideration. Questions about the position should be emailed to Dr. Rich Devine (Search Committee Chair) at rdevine2@depaul.edu . The required qualifications are a Doctoral degree in Strategic Management or related field. ABD candidates will be considered. Prior university teaching experience in areas of strategic management, business policy, or corporate strategy is preferred. Candidates with industry experience are welcome. Candidates will need to submit the following materials as a part of their application: A cover letter stating interest and qualification A curriculum vitae Research Statement Teaching Statement Teaching evaluations, if applicable Sample publications, if applicable Contact information for three professional references. Confidential letters of recommendation may be requested from those individuals. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188855": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor (Tenure Track) and Coleman Endowed Chair - Management & Entrepreneurship (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: DRIEHAUS COLLEGE OF BUSINESS: MANAGEMENT & ENTREPRENEURSHIP Location: Chicago, IL - Driehaus College of Business The Coleman Endowed Chair in Entrepreneurship primary responsibilities will be to provide strong research and curricular leadership for our entrepreneurship programs, including graduate degree programs (MBA, Doctorate in Business Administration) and undergraduate major and minor degree offerings, interface with the Coleman Center and its stakeholders, and cultivate and maintain effective relationships with internal advisory boards and Chicago’s thriving entrepreneurship ecosystem.  Other responsibilities may include providing guidance to doctoral students pursuing research in the field of entrepreneurship. The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship houses a diverse, multi-disciplinary and research-active faculty who support undergraduate and graduate programs in entrepreneurship, business analytics, human resource management, general management, supply chain management, and sustainability management.  Management and Entrepreneurship faculty research has appeared in top-ranked journals, including Academy of Management Journal, Journal of Applied Psychology, Journal of Management, Journal of Business Venturing, and Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice. Both the graduate and undergraduate entrepreneurship programs were nationally ranked in the top-20 by The Princeton Review.  The department is also home to the Coleman Center for Entrepreneurship, which received the 2023 Nasdaq Award for Entrepreneurial Excellence.  A number of active student groups, including a chapter of the Collegiate Entrepreneurs’ Organization, are affiliated with the department. Located in the center of Chicago's downtown, DePaul's Driehaus College of Business immerses students in one of the world's great business centers to provide transformative, hands-on educational experiences. Enrolling over 5,400 students, Driehaus's undergraduate and graduate programs are highly ranked and nationally recognized. Founded in 1912, Driehaus was among the first 10 business colleges in the United States and the first at an American Catholic university. The Driehaus mission is to empower students to become socially responsible leaders who make an impact in their communities. Guided by our Catholic and Vincentian values and aided by our deep roots in the City of Chicago, we deliver a cutting-edge business education, generate pathbreaking research, and collaborate closely with our community and industry partners to drive positive social outcomes. Visit https://business.depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx The Department of Management and Entrepreneurship at DePaul University’s Driehaus College of Business invites outstanding scholars to apply for the Coleman Endowed Chair in Entrepreneurship at the rank of Associate or Full Professor. We seek an internationally recognized scholar and proven educator to enhance the ranks of our faculty by bringing a strong and active research record along with the expertise and perspectives gained from a notable academic career.  Applicants must have a doctorate in entrepreneurship or a related field. The successful candidate must qualify for the rank of Associate or Full Professor with tenure and be a nationally recognized scholar in entrepreneurship.  Required qualifications include an outstanding record of publications in top entrepreneurship and management academic journals, evidence of teaching excellence, and notable service contributions.  Candidates will also be expected to demonstrate the ability to work collegially and collaboratively within the academic and business communities. Applicants will need to submit the following materials as part of their application: A cover letter stating interest and qualification A curriculum vitae Teaching statement Research statement Sample publications Teaching evaluations Contact information for three professional references. Confidential letters of recommendation may be requested from those individuals. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188849": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Finance (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: DRIEHAUS COLLEGE OF BUSINESS: FINANCE Location: Chicago, IL - Driehaus College of Business The Department of Finance and Real Estate in the Driehaus College of Business at DePaul University invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in finance in all areas of specialty and at the rank of Assistant Professor. Located in the center of Chicago's downtown, DePaul’s Driehaus College of Business immerses students in one of the world’s great business centers to provide transformative, hands-on educational experiences. Enrolling over 5,400 students, Driehaus’s undergraduate and graduate programs are highly ranked and nationally recognized. Founded in 1912, Driehaus was among the first 10 business colleges in the United States and the first at an American Catholic university. The Driehaus mission is to empower students to become socially responsible leaders who make an impact in their communities. Guided by our Catholic and Vincentian values and aided by our deep roots in the City of Chicago, we deliver a cutting-edge business education, generate pathbreaking research, and collaborate closely with our community and industry partners to drive positive social outcomes. Visit https://business.depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx . Responsibilities Deliver high-quality undergraduate and graduate courses in the various areas of finance. Develop and maintain an active research agenda that results in quality journal publications. Collaborate with colleagues and actively contribute to the intellectual life of the department. Participate in service activities at all levels (departmental, college, and university-level). Contribute to the support of the department's student recruitment and retention efforts. Contribute to the overall success of the department and college by participating in workshops, events, and other relevant activities. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Finance, Economics, or a related field. Demonstrated potential for making significant contributions to the field of finance. Strong teaching skills and a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education. Interested candidates should submit 1. Cover Letter detailing interest in the position 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Names and contact information of three individuals prepared to provide letters of recommendation 4. A representative sample of teaching evaluations (if available) 5. Research paper(s) General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188893": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Anthropology (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: ANTHROPOLOGY Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Anthropology Department at DePaul University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in cultural anthropology to begin September 1, 2027. We seek a cultural anthropologist doing theoretically informed, community-engaged research. Geographical area is open but should complement the current department faculty coverage. Topical areas of focus may include but are not limited to environmental anthropology; political ecology; climate change; sustainability; the anthropocene; or critical Indigenous studies. Applicants should offer evidence of ethnographically grounded research, clear plans for future scholarship, and demonstrated excellence in teaching. We are especially interested in candidates who have a capacity for mentoring students with diverse research interests and are eager to collaborate across a wide set of area studies programs on campus. The Department of Anthropology ofers an undergraduate major, which provides a broad foundation in four-field anthropology, along with two minors. We also participate in three additional interdisciplinary minor programs in our college. DePaul operates on the quarter system, with tenure-line faculty teaching six courses per academic year. Teaching responsibilities will include courses that contribute to the department programs and to the university’s First Year and Liberal Studies Programs. Required Ph.D. in Cultural Anthropology by time of application Demonstrated excellence in teaching and experience teaching cultural anthropology in a college or university setting Ability to teach core courses for the major that draw on all four subfields of anthropology A record of, or clear potential for, scholarly research leading to publications and conference presentations A record of, or clear potential for, service to the university and the profession Ability to contribute to program growth, curricular innovation, and student advising Preferred Ability to teach courses in linguistic anthropology Ability to develop community-based, project-learning courses in the city of Chicago To apply, please submit: a cover letter; curriculum vitae; a statement of teaching philosophy addressing the candidate’s teaching experience and interests; and contact information for three references. All materials should be submitted electronically using Interfolio. Confidential letters of recommendation will be requested later in the recruitment process for semi-finalists. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Rachel Scott, Department and Search Committee Chair, at rachel.scott@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188845": {
      "title": "Term Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) - Biological Sciences (26-27)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF SCIENCE & HEALTH: BIOLOGICAL SCIENCES Location: Chicago, IL - College of Science and Health The Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a term (non-tenure track) faculty position as a Teaching Assistant Professor with teaching responsibilities commencing January 1, 2027 and finishing June 30, 2027. Subject to successful reappointment, we anticipate the position will continue with a 10-month contract (Sept. 1 – June 30). We seek candidates with a demonstrated record of effectiveness or potential for success as both a laboratory coordinator and (lab/lecture) instructor for biology courses and a commitment to continued development as an educator. Responsibilities will include coordinating labs for large, multi-section courses in the General Biology core sequence, teaching lab/lecture in General Biology, as well as teaching courses and lab sections for science majors, non-science majors, and/or graduate students. The area of applicant specialization should be in at least one of the following areas: cellular and molecular biology or anatomy and physiology. The specific courses will depend on the area of applicant specialization and departmental need. Providing mentoring for course-based undergraduate student research and working with the Center for Teaching and Learning for continued professional development are also possibilities for motivated individuals. Visit https://csh.depaul.edu/academics/biological-sciences/Pages/default.aspx for more information about the Department of Biological Sciences. Required A MS or higher degree in a biological field At least one year of teaching at the college level Preferred A PhD in a biological field At least one year of teaching at the college level as the instructor of record Applicants should submit a full and complete application that includes: A cover letter Curriculum vita Statement of teaching philosophy that addresses the instructor’s experience, perspectives, and goals in teaching students with a range of scientific experience and academic preparation Contact information for three professional references who will be contacted through the Interfolio system for a letter of reference Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Candidates will not be considered until all the above materials are received. For additional questions about this position, please e-mail Dr. Joanna Brooke, Biological Sciences Search Committee and Department Chair at jbrooke@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188882": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Modern Languages, Japanese (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: MODERN LANGUAGES Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Department of Modern Languages in the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences at DePaul University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Japanese, beginning in Fall 2027. DePaul’s interdisciplinary Japanese Studies program offers a major and a curriculum that integrates advanced Japanese-language study with area studies courses in Japanese culture, literature, history, religion, art, politics, and related fields. The successful candidate will serve as Director of the Japanese Studies Program and coordinate the Japanese-language curriculum. Teaching responsibilities will include Japanese-language courses at all levels; courses in Japanese linguistics, translation, Foreign Languages Across the Curriculum (FLAC), culture, and literature; and teaching in the First-Year and Liberal Studies Programs. The candidate will be expected to maintain a rigorous and productive research agenda leading to peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, and other scholarly contributions appropriate to the candidate’s field. Additional responsibilities will include supervising study-abroad and international internship programs; serving as the content-area advisor for the Japanese concentration in World Language Education in the College of Education; advising students; contributing to curriculum development and program growth; and providing leadership for community-engaged initiatives with local educational, cultural, and business organizations. ● Ph.D. in Japanese linguistics, second-language acquisition, language pedagogy, Japanese literature, or a closely related field. ● Demonstrated excellence in teaching and experience teaching Japanese language at multiple levels in a college or university setting. ● A record of, or clear potential for, scholarly research leading to publications and conference presentations. ● A record of, or clear potential for, service to the university, the profession, and relevant academic organizations ● Evidence of the ability to contribute to program growth, curricular innovation, student advising, and interdisciplinary collaboration. ● Near-native or native proficiency in Japanese and English to carry out the teaching, advising, and administrative responsibilities of the position. 1. A cover letter describing the applicant’s qualifications and relevant experience. 2. A curriculum vitae 3. A statement of teaching philosophy*. 4. A statement describing the applicant’s research agenda*. 5. Three letters of recommendation * Applicants may also submit evidence of effective teaching, including student teaching evaluations, awards and sample syllabi, and evidence of research, including scholarly works such as peer-reviewed journal articles, dissertation chapters, etc. Reviews of eligible applicants will begin on November 1, 2026, and continue until the position has been filled. Only complete applications will be considered. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Nobuko Chikamatsu, Chair of the Search Committee, at nchikama@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188880": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Philosophy (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: PHILOSOPHY Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences We are hiring someone at the Assistant Professor level who specializes in the work of Martin Heidegger. We are interested in a scholar with expertise across the Heideggerian corpus , who will contribute to our general departmental focus on Continental Philosophy. We are seeking someone who can effectively place Heidegger in conversation with, and complement our existing strengths in, one or more of these areas: Latin American philosophy, ethics, political philosophy, psychoanalysis, phenomenology, and the history of philosophy. Our Philosophy Department currently has 15 members and offers the B.A., M.A., and Ph.D. degrees. Candidates must have a demonstrable proficiency in relevant languages and will be expected to teach in DePaul's Liberal Studies Program/First-Year Program, Opportunities also exist to work with DePaul's many programs and institutes, such as the Women’s and Gender Studies Program, the Institute for Business and Professional Ethics, the Comparative Literature Program, the Center for Latino Research, the Chinese Studies Program, and the African and Black Diaspora Studies Program. Preference will be given to candidates with a Ph.D., but advanced ABDs will be considered if degree conferral is expected by the start date. Applications, including a cover letter, a dissertation abstract, current C.V., a teaching statement, three letters of recommendation, and a writing sample, should be electronically submitted in Interfolio.  For full consideration, please submit application materials by November 18th. We anticipate Zoom interviews to begin in December with on campus interviews in January 2027, however, applications will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188844": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Psychology, Industrial-Organizational (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF SCIENCE & HEALTH: PSYCHOLOGY Location: Chicago, IL - College of Science and Health The Department of Psychology at DePaul University invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor in Industrial-Organizational (I-O) Psychology to begin in September 2027. DePaul's Department of Psychology has an I-O undergraduate concentration, an MS, and an MA/PhD program as well as a host of other undergraduate and graduate programs. The selected candidate is expected to develop and maintain a productive research program, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and direct undergraduate and graduate student research including theses and PhD dissertations in I-O. Candidates must be able to teach one or more of the following graduate courses: Personnel Psychology Psychology of Leadership Work Teams and Collaboration More information about the Department of Psychology is available at: https://csh.depaul.edu/academics/psychology/Pages/default.aspx . Competitive candidates will have a PhD in Industrial-Organizational Psychology, a strong research record, and evidence of, or potential for, teaching and mentoring excellence. For full consideration, applicants must complete the online application which includes the following: Cover letter (no more than 2 pages) detailing interest in the position and area(s) for potential teaching and training contributions at the undergraduate and graduate level Curriculum vitae highlighting (a) education and qualifications; (b) teaching experience (if applicable); (c) research accomplishments; and (d) service contributions (if applicable) Research statement (no more than 2 pages) highlighting significant theoretical and/or applied interests and contributions, and methodological strengths Representative reprints and/or preprints (no more than 3) Teaching statement (no more than 2 pages) highlighting list of teaching interests at undergraduate and graduate level, mentoring philosophy, and pedagogical approaches and innovations Teaching evaluations (if available) Contact information for three professional references who will be contacted by the Interfolio application system for direct recommendation letter uploads Application materials will be reviewed beginning Thursday, October 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Please contact Dr. Shelly Rauvola ( rrauvola@depaul.edu ) and Dr. Alice Stuhlmacher ( astuhlma@depaul.edu ), Search Committee Co-chairs, with questions about the position. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188884": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - School of Public Service (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: SCHOOL OF PUBLIC SERVICE Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The School of Public Service (SPS) in the College of Liberal Arts & Social Sciences at DePaul University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development, growth, and evaluation of SPS through excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and student-centered academic leadership. This position supports SPS’s Master of Public Policy (MPP) and Master in Public Administration (MPA) graduate programs, as well as its undergraduate BA in Public Policy degree. The courses taught by the faculty members, however, will also include students from other degree programs as listed below. We seek candidates with expertise for teaching introductory courses in public administration and public policy, practitioner-focused research methods and program evaluation, and capstone courses. Among other secondary areas of focus are government financial management and applied statistics. SPS also seeks a scholar educator who is committed to meaningful student engagement, a focused and sustainable program of scholarship, and service to the School, College, University, profession, and community. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to preparing students for careers in public policy and public administration. The successful candidate will be expected to: Provide high-quality and didactic classroom instruction to both graduate and undergraduate students. Engage in course development, course revision, syllabus preparation, instructional design, competency-based teaching strategies, assessment of student learning outcomes, and use of educational technologies that support student success. Contribute to the MPA and MPP programs’ quality through participation in accreditation-related activities, systematic evaluation, course assessment, program assessment, and continuous quality improvement processes. Support student success initiatives, including career mentoring and support of classroom-based research projects Develop and maintain a focused, sustainable program of scholarship appropriate to a tenure-track appointment, including peer-reviewed dissemination, presentations, and pursuit of internal or external funding as appropriate. Serve on School, College, and University committees and contribute to shared governance, strategic initiatives, and the ongoing advancement of SPS. Demonstrate leadership within SPS and the community through teaching, scholarship, service, and engagement. About the School of Public Service DePaul University’s School of Service, on DePaul’s Loop Campus, offers five degrees: MPA, MPP, Master in Nonprofit Management, M.S. in International Public Service, and M.S. in Public Service Management (an executive program), as well as the undergraduate BA in Public Policy.  It also offers non-degree curricular certificates and extracurricular programs in partnership with the M.A. in Sustainable Urban Development and Chaddick Institute for Metropolitan Development. Required qualifications A Ph.D. in public policy, public administration, or a related field, or plans for imminent completion of such a degree Evidence of potential for effective teaching, scholarship, and service appropriate to a tenure-track faculty appointment Demonstrated commitment to student success Preferred qualifications Experience teaching both graduate and undergraduate students Evidence of scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed publications, presentations, funded projects, or a developing research agenda Experience with syllabus preparation and assessment of student learning outcomes or continuous quality improvement A complete application should contain the following: Letter of application describing interest in the position, qualifications, teaching experience, scholarly interests, and alignment with DePaul University and the School of Public Service Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of scholarship or research agenda Contact information for three professional references. References may be contacted through the application system to upload letters of recommendation directly. Candidates will not be considered until all required materials are received. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications submitted by October 1, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Interviews are anticipated to begin in November. Questions about the position may be directed to: Dr. Joseph Schwieterman, Chair of Search Committee and Degree Chair of the MPA program at jschwiet@depaul.edu General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188899": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Religious Studies (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: RELIGIOUS STUDIES Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Department of Religious Studies at DePaul University invites applicants for a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning September 2027. We are looking for a candidate who specializes in Hebrew Scriptures. The successful candidate will demonstrate advanced proficiency in Biblical Hebrew and one or more other ancient languages relevant to the study of the Hebrew Bible (e.g.Ugaritic, Akkadian, Aramaic, or Greek), bringing rigorous textual, theological, and historical analysis to the classroom. They should also be prepared to teach thematic courses, such as Women in the Bible and Ancient Israel: History, Literature, and Religion, as well as a willingness to expand the department’s offerings in Hebrew Bible and to teach in cross-disciplinary programs. We are interested in applicants from Religious Studies and allied disciplines whose research and teaching complement the interests and strengths of our interdisciplinary Department. Preference will be given to candidates with a Ph.D., but advanced ABDs will be considered if degree conferral is expected by the start date. For full consideration please send a letter of application, curriculum vitae, a research statement, a recent writing sample, one sample syllabus, and the names and email addresses of three references to the Search Committee by October 16, 2026. Confidential letters of recommendation will be requested for shortlisted candidates. Review of applications will begin immediately, and preliminary interviews of shortlisted candidates will be conducted via Zoom. If you have any questions, please contact Dr. Lisa Poirier, the chair of the search committee at lpoirier@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188895": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Criminology (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: CRIMINOLOGY Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Criminology Department invites applications for a tenure-track, assistant professor appointment for the Academic Year 2027-2028, specialization open. Preferred candidates will be those able and willing to teach both in-person and online; one or more core required courses; elective courses in their area of specialization; and contribute to the first-year Liberal Studies Program. The Criminology Department at DePaul University is a rapidly growing undergraduate major in the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences. Located on DePaul’s Lincoln Park campus in Chicago, the Department provides students with an in-depth understanding of the various aspects of the criminal legal system, emphasizing courses that examine community justice; criminal justice administration; and race, class, gender, and the criminal legal system. DePaul’s Criminology major emphasizes critical thinking, strong analytical and writing skills, ethical considerations, and social justice. The preferred candidate will have a Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related field, with effective teaching and research experience in criminology or criminal justice. ABD candidates with significant progress toward dissertation completion and individuals with lived experiences are encouraged to apply. The search involves a two-step process: a Zoom interview and an on-campus interview. Candidates invited to an on-campus interview will be asked to complete two presentations to students and faculty: one research and one teaching presentation. Successful applications will be required to support the Department and the University’s mission through teaching, scholarship and research activities, and service. Teaching expectations include: supporting student learning, retention, persistence, and program completion; completing professional development; teaching assigned courses that may include day, evening, online, or hybrid courses; teaching at the Lincoln Park campus or online as needed; posting and holding office hours; maintaining and improving competence in the subjects taught; and advising students about career opportunities. Scholarly or research expectations include: conducting research or producing scholarly works in criminology or criminal justice, including community-engaged scholarship or applied research; seeking opportunities to engage students in research activities; presenting at professionally recognized venues; and sharing one’s scholarship and research activities through peer review journals or other professionally recognized publication types. Service expectations include: supporting student organizations or activities; participating in Department, College, and University committees; supporting local, state, national agencies or communities through research or other service activities; and participating in leadership positions with professional or community organizations. A complete application contains the following: a cover letter indicating your interest and qualification for the position, including any personal statements related to teaching, research-scholarship, and service, curriculum vita, and three reference letters. Applicants may also submit evidence of effective teaching, including student teaching reviews, and evidence of research, including scholarly works such as peer-reviewed journal articles, dissertation chapters, etc. Reviews of eligible applicants will begin on September 15, 2026, and continue until the position has been filled. Only complete applications will be considered, and priority will be given to those applications submitted by September 15, 2026. Questions about this position can be directed to Dr. Megan Alderden, Department Chair, at megan.alderden@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188840": {
      "title": "Term Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) - Jaharis Health Law Faculty Fellow (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LAW: LAW ACADEMIC Location: Chicago, IL - College of Law The Jaharis Health Law Institute is accepting applications for a Faculty Fellow in Health Law and Intellectual Property/Information Technology expected to begin on August 1, 2027. Established in 1984 and supported by the Mary and Michael Jaharis Health Law Institute (JHLI), DePaul’s health law program has consistently ranked among the top in the nation. JHLI offers students coursework that reflects the diversity of health law from community health to high-tech health care, making DePaul a leader in the education of future generations of health law partners, policy makers and critical thinkers. The fellowship is designed to encourage scholars interested in entering a career in legal academia in the fields of Health Law and IP/IT. The Fellow will be expected to: Teach curricular offerings at the intersection of health & IP/IT; Write and present scholarly work in health & IP/IT; Supervise and advise JD, LLM and MLS students in these areas; Support the work of CIPLIT® and JHLI. The appointment will be for one academic year, with the possibility of extending for one additional year. JD degree or equivalent Excellent writing skills Either relevant job experience or relevant scholarly work at the intersection of health law and IP/IT Interested candidates should apply online via DePaul's Faculty Jobs Portal. Required materials include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, list of three (3) contact references, research statement, and writing sample. Questions concerning the Jaharis Faculty Fellowship should be sent to Professor Valerie Koch, Chair of 2026-2027 Jaharis Faculty Fellow Hiring Committee ( vkoch1@depaul.edu ). General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188842": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - Law (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LAW: LAW ACADEMIC Location: Chicago, IL - College of Law DePaul University College of Law invites applications from entry-level and junior-lateral (0-3 years) candidates for a tenure-track position expected to begin July 1, 2027. We are looking for candidates to teach in Property Law and/or Family Law. At DePaul Law, we are dedicated to producing purpose-driven lawyers who serve the public with integrity and compassion. Our graduates embrace a tradition of service to others and work tirelessly to enhance access to the legal system for the most vulnerable members of our society. To learn more about us, please visit https://law.depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx . All candidates must hold a J.D. or equivalent degree, possess excellent academic credentials, and demonstrate potential to be an outstanding scholar and teacher. Interested candidates should apply online via DePaul's Faculty Jobs Portal. Required materials include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, list of three (3) contact references, research statement, and writing sample. Please direct any questions about the position to the Chair of the appointments committee at mbedi@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/63936": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, College of Law - General Doctrinal Courses",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF LAW - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Law The College of Law invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching opportunities  within the following general doctrinal areas: - Administrative Law - Business Law - Compliance and Regulatory Law - Criminal Law and Procedure - Family Law - Evidence - General Practice - Health Law - Intellectual Property Law - International Law - Labor and Employment - Practice Management - Real Estate and Property Law - Tax Law - Trusts and Estates Applications are reviewed as needed when positions arise. In order to best serve the students, part-time faculty are expected to perform all duties and responsibilities of a faculty member that are commensurate and consistent with the faculty member's qualifications and the best interests of DePaul. JD degree or an equivalent advanced degree in a relevant subject. Demonstrated expertise in a particular area of law or legal study. Please visit the College of Law website to learn more about our program: http://law.depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enrolled or under-enrolled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers a variety of benefit options for qualified part-time employees. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/part-time/Pages/default.aspx About DePaul University's Academic Calendar: Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length. The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
