    "https://apply.interfolio.com/63938": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, College of Law - Legal Writing Program",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF LAW - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Law The College of Law invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching opportunities within the Legal Analysis, Research and Communication program (LARC). The College of Law offers legal drafting courses in the following areas: -Civil Litigation -Child and Family Law -Criminal Law -Health Law -Intellectual Property -Real Estate -Transactions -Trusts & Estates Opportunities are also available to teach general and advanced LARC courses, including appellate brief writing and oral advocacy. Applications are reviewed as needed when positions arise. In order to best serve students, part-time faculty are expected to perform all duties and responsibilities of a faculty member that are commensurate and consistent with the faculty member's qualifications and the best interests of DePaul. JD degree and at least 5 years of professional experience in the legal field. Demonstrated expertise in a particular area of law or legal study. Please visit the College of Law website to learn more about our program: http://law.depaul.edu/Pages/default.aspx Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enrolled or under-enrolled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers a