    "https://apply.interfolio.com/64018": {
      "title": "Part Time Faculty, The Art School",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES - PT: THE ART SCHOOL -  PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Art School, within the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences at DePaul University, invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching. Part-time teaching opportunities fluctuate from quarter to quarter throughout the academic year. The applicants with expertise that match the course scheduling needs will be contacted for an interview. The School will work with selected individuals to determine their schedule. Courses are not guaranteed; however, the School does its best to give ample notice about available classes or potential course cancellations. – a cover letter indicating teaching experience and interests. – a current CV, MFA in Art, or a related area – 2 years of teaching experience is required. This could include an instructor of record position while in graduate school. – Experience teaching at a university or liberal arts college preferred. – Examples of their artwork, and student work-if available (Which can be a website) – list of three professional references – 2 examples of syllabi and corresponding student evaluations The applicant’s schedule must be flexible to accommodate quarterly course schedules (studio block meets for 2 hours and 45 minutes, twice a week, M/W, TU/TH). This posting applies to the following sub-disciplinary specialties: Studio Art (Drawing, Painting, Printmaking, Sculpture, and Digital Imaging in Studio Art) Photography and Media Art (Photography, Digital Photography, Intermedia/Web Art, and Video Art) Graphic Art Please visit the following URL for information about the program and course offerings: art-media-design.depaul.edu . Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses tha