    "https://apply.interfolio.com/64032": {
      "title": "Part Time Faculty, Criminology Program",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES - PT: CRIMINOLOGY - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Criminology program within the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences at DePaul University invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching opportunities. Part-time teaching opportunities are available throughout the academic year. This position is ideal for practitioners, researchers, and experienced educators seeking to contribute to the academic development of undergraduate students in criminology and criminal justice. Courses are not guaranteed as academic course schedules fluctuate from quarter to quarter; however, the program does its best to give ample notice about available courses and potential course cancellations. Part-time faculty typically teach one to two classes an academic year. Applicants with expertise that matches course scheduling needs will be contacted for an interview. MA/MS in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or closely related fields and/or JD for specific courses. Preference will be given to applicants with a PhD in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or closely related field. This posting applies to all courses in Criminology, but particularly elective courses offered by the Department. Please visit the following URL for information about the program and course offerings: https://las.depaul.edu/academics/criminology/Pages/default.aspx Required Applicant Documents C.V. Cover Letter Teaching Statement Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enrolled or under-enrolled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. 