    "https://apply.interfolio.com/64011": {
      "title": "Part Time Faculty, English",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES - PT: ENGLISH - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Department of English within the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences at DePaul University invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching opportunities, should they become available during the academic year. Applicants with expertise that matches course scheduling needs will be contacted for an interview if courses become available. Academic course schedules fluctuate from quarter to quarter and the department will work with selected individuals to determine a quarterly schedule. The Department does its best to give ample notice about available courses and potential course cancellations. Please note: If you are interested in teaching composition courses, you should apply to the Writing, Rhetoric, and Discourse Department. Master's Degree in English Literature and/or Creative Writing, or three years of experience in the publishing industry. Experience teaching literature and/or creative writing courses at the college level strongly preferred. This posting applies to the following areas: -British Literature -American Literature -Multiethnic Literature -Creative Writing -Publishing Applicants whose qualifications meet current needs may be asked to submit further materials. Please visit the following URL for information about the program and course offerings: https://las.depaul.edu/academics/english/about/Pages/default.aspx Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enrolled or under-enrolled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting.