      "title": "Part Time Faculty, School of Public Service",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES - PT: SCHOOL OF PUBLIC SERVICE - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The School of Public Service within the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences at DePaul University invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching opportunities at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. Graduate and undergraduate part-time teaching opportunities are available throughout the academic year in subject areas such as public policy, international development and public service, public administration, nonprofit management, and government finance. Academic course schedules fluctuate from quarter to quarter and the School will work with selected individuals to determine a quarterly schedule. Courses are not guaranteed; however the Department does its best to give ample notice about available courses and potential course cancellations. Applicants with expertise that matches course scheduling needs will be contacted for an interview. For more information about the School of Public Service’s BA in Public Policy, and Masters programs see: https://las.depaul.edu/academics/school-of-public-service/Pages/default.aspx For teaching at the graduate level: Ph.D./J.D./D.P.A. degree, or Masters degree and substantial professional experience in fields relevant to the School of Public Service academic programs. For teaching at the undergraduate level: MA in Public Policy or related field. If candidate does not possess an MA in related field then an MA and relevant work experience greater than two years. When applying please upload the following: CV Cover Letter Names and contact details for two references Additional Documents Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enrolled or u