      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF SCIENCE & HEALTH - PT: HEALTH SCIENCES - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Science and Health The Department of Health Sciences within the College of Science and Health at DePaul University invites expressions of interest in part-time faculty teaching opportunities at the undergraduate (Bachelor of Science) and graduate (Master of Public Health) level for the 2026-2027 Academic Year. This posting applies to the following sub-disciplines: Public Health Health Care Policy Epidemiology Global Health Program Evaluation Community Needs Assessment Health Ethics Microbiology Anatomy and Physiology Nutrition Medical Terminology Health Careers Health Behavior Theory Related Courses Applicants interested in teaching in any of the areas specified in this posting are invited to apply, and those with qualifications matching department’s scheduling needs will be contacted for an interview. A PhD or equivalent degree in a health sciences-related field (public health, biology, anthropology, bioethics, etc.) or a Master’s degree in a health sciences-related field and at least 5 years of work experience in addition to previous teaching experience are required. Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enroled or under-enrolled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, an