    "https://apply.interfolio.com/187284": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - School of Nursing: BSN (26-27)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF SCIENCE & HEALTH: SCHOOL OF NURSING: BSN Location: Chicago, IL - College of Science and Health The School of Nursing in the College of Science and Health at DePaul University invites applications for a full time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor in the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development, growth, and evaluation of the BSN program through excellence in teaching, scholarship, service, and student-centered academic leadership. This position supports the School of Nursing’s strategic priorities related to program quality, student success, licensure readiness, inclusive excellence, simulation and technology integration, accreditation readiness, community engagement, and faculty scholarship. The faculty member will teach primarily in the BSN program and will contribute to the preparation of undergraduate nursing students for safe, ethical, evidence based, compassionate, and equity centered professional nursing practice. The School of Nursing seeks a scholar educator who is committed to high quality teaching, meaningful student engagement, a focused and sustainable program of scholarship, and service to the School, College, University, profession, and community. Candidates should demonstrate a strong commitment to the preparation of nurses who are equipped to advance health equity. Job Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Provide high quality didactic, clinical, and laboratory instruction primarily in the BSN program, with attention to clinical judgment, safe nursing practice, inclusive teaching, and student progression toward licensure readiness. Engage in course development, course revision, syllabus preparation, instructional design, competency-based teaching strategies, assessment of student learning outcomes, and use of educational technologies that support student success. Contribute to BSN program quality through participation in accreditation related activities, systematic evaluation, course assessment, program assessment, and continuous quality improvement processes. Support student success initiatives, including progression support, remediation, clinical judgment development, NCLEX readiness, and evaluation of learning outcomes. Serve as lead faculty for assigned courses as appropriate and provide mentorship, guidance, and support to adjunct faculty teaching within the BSN program. Develop and maintain a focused, sustainable program of scholarship appropriate to a tenure track appointment, including peer reviewed dissemination, presentations, and pursuit of internal or external funding as appropriate. Advise and mentor undergraduate nursing students in support of academic progression, professional formation, belonging, and preparation for nursing practice. Serve on School, College, and University committees and contribute to shared governance, strategic initiatives, and the ongoing advancement of the School of Nursing. Demonstrate leadership within the School of Nursing, College of Science and Health, University, profession, and community through teaching, scholarship, service, and engagement. About the School of Nursing DePaul University’s School of Nursing offers BSN, Master’s Entry into Nursing Practice, RN to MSN-Specialty, Post-Master Certificate, and DNP programs. Programs within the School of Nursing emphasize academic excellence, clinical judgment, community engagement, service learning, health equity, social justice, and the preparation of nurses who provide safe, high-quality, person-centered care. Students complete clinical learning experiences across more than 100 health care institutions. About the College of Science and Health The College of Science and Health includes the School of Nursing and departments of Biological Sciences, Chemistry and Biochemistry, Environmental Science and Studies, Health Sciences, Mathematical Sciences, Neuroscience, Physics and Astrophysics, Psychology, and Rehabilitative Sciences and Professions. The College of Science and Health is committed to delivering exceptional, personalized, accessible, and inclusive education in science and health disciplines to a diverse student body. Rooted in the enduring values of St. Vincent de Paul, we nurture student success and a sense of belonging within our community. As leaders in science and health education and research in the vibrant city of Chicago, we embrace our responsibility to promote social and environmental justice. Required qualifications Doctoral degree in nursing or a related field Graduate degree in nursing if the doctoral degree is in a related field Current RN license in Illinois, or eligibility for Illinois RN licensure with application in process by the time of appointment Minimum of two years of clinical nursing experience Evidence of potential for effective teaching, scholarship, and service appropriate to a tenure track faculty appointment Demonstrated commitment to student success Preferred qualifications Experience teaching BSN or prelicensure nursing students Teaching or clinical expertise in medical surgical nursing, pediatrics, community or public health, maternal child health, mental health, or another area aligned with BSN curricular needs Experience with laboratory teaching, clinical judgment development, competency-based education, or educational technology Evidence of scholarly productivity, including peer reviewed publications, presentations, funded projects, or a developing research agenda Experience with accreditation, curriculum development, assessment of student learning outcomes, NCLEX readiness, or continuous quality improvement Commitment to health equity and interprofessional education A complete application should contain the following: Letter of application describing interest in the position, qualifications, teaching experience, scholarly interests, and alignment with DePaul University and the School of Nursing mission Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of scholarship or research agenda Contact information for three professional references. References may be contacted through the application system to upload letters of recommendation directly. Candidates will not be considered until all required materials are received. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications submitted by July 17, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Interviews are anticipated to begin in July. Questions about the position may be directed to: Dr. Roxanne Spurlark, Director of the School of Nursing rspurlar@depaul.edu . General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar: Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/117609": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Office of Innovative Professional Learning",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST - Adjunct: COLLEGE OF EDUCATION - PT: OFFICE OF INNOVATIVE PROFESSIONAL LEARNING - PT Location: Chicago, IL - College of Education The Office of Innovative Professional Learning (OIPL) in the College of Education invites expressions of interest for part-time faculty teaching opportunities for the 2025-2026 Academic Year. OIPL provides schools and organizations individualized and customized professional development, coaching, or mentoring that relies on best practices. Adjunct teaching opportunities are available throughout the academic year, including summer sessions. Applicants with expertise that matches with the current projects of the office will be contacted for an interview. Projects fluctuate from quarter to quarter and selected individuals will work with the Office of Innovative Professional Learning on a per project basis. Projects are not guaranteed; however the Office does its best to give ample notice about available opportunities and potential cancellations. The Office of Innovative Professional Learning seeks applicants with expertise and experience in the following areas: -Our students represent many different perspectives and cultures, and the university strives to recruit and sustain a faculty community where all backgrounds are valued and supported. -Training teachers in best Practices in Teaching Practice Areas including: -Curriculum design -Student engagement -Assessment -Content area integration -Data driven instruction - International Baccalaureate Programs (PYP, MYP, DP and Leadership Practice) - Leadership development - Teaching in international contexts - STEAM and STEM Education - Counseling, psychology, and/or neuroscience as it relates to teaching - Trauma informed teaching - Many other areas as well Applications are reviewed year-round for this part-time adjunct position. Questions about the application process for this role with OIPL should be sent to: Dr. Donna Kiel Director of Office of Innovative Professional Learning INNOVATE@depaul.edu Considerations: Exceptions to standard rates may apply to courses with unique credit hours, supervision, labs, clinical/practicum courses, coaching, administrative tasks, and courses that are either over-enroled or under-enrolled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement: DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers a variety of benefit options for qualified part-time employees. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/part-time/Pages/default.aspx About DePaul University's Academic Calendar: Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length. The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188897": {
      "title": "Term Faculty (Non-Tenure Track) - The Art School (26-27)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: ART MEDIA AND DESIGN Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences The Art School, part of DePaul University's College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences in Chicago, Illinois, invites applications for a for a full-time Term faculty position in Photography and Media Art , beginning January 1 , 2027 . A Term faculty position carries the following responsibilities: Teaching : Teach 3 undergraduate classes each of the two quarters (winter 2027 and spring 2027) in digital photography, analog photography and in video art within The Art School. Creative Practice: Produce and exhibit high-quality artwork and/or engage in related creative activities. Located in Chicago’s Lincoln Park neighborhood, The Art School at DePaul University offers three degree programs: § BA in Art § BA in Art, Media, and Design § BFA in Art, Media, and Design The school also offers seven minors/shared minors in art. Teaching and creative spaces/studios include dedicated painting, drawing, printmaking, photography (darkroom and digital), sculpture studios, and digital computer studios. Professional Background: Candidates must be a practicing artist with an established record of exhibition/creative activities and experience in digital photography, analog photography and video art. Education: A Master of Fine Arts (MFA) in photography, video or other photography and media arts. Teaching Experience: A minimum of 2 years of college/university-level teaching experience completed after graduate school (excluding any graduate-level teaching experience). This experience can include full-time term, part-time, or other related faculty positions at the college/university level. Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. 1. Professional Materials , submit the following: - Cover Letter detailing your interest in the position, and your qualifications - Curriculum Vitae - 20 examples of current studio artwork focused on photography and/or other media arts, with any accompanying list of works submitted (including media, size, and year completed) 2. Syllabi , submit the following: - Two syllabi from courses you have taught in photography (analog and digital, and video art). 3. Student Work Samples , submit the following: - 20 examples of student work in relationship to the submitted syllabi 4. List of three (3) contacts for teaching references. Confidential Letters of recommendation will be requested through the Interfolio system later in the recruitment process for semi-finalists. For full consideration, please submit application materials by November 6th. We anticipate Zoom interviews to begin shortly thereafter with on campus interviews before the end of November, however, applications will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188896": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure Track) - History (27-28)",
      "description": "Department: DePaul University: PROVOST: COLLEGE OF LIBERAL ARTS AND SCIENCES: HISTORY Location: Chicago, IL - College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences Posted: Oct 22, 2026 Deadline: Dec 15, 2026 DePaul University invites applications for an assistant professor specializing in Modern Chinese history with an expertise in International Studies, for a tenure track position for the 2027-28 academic year. While the position will be housed in the History Department, the candidate will teach in both the History Department and International Studies.  The faculty will also be expected to teach in the University’s interdisciplinary programs like the Chicago Quarter, Honors, and Study Abroad. The candidate must have a PhD in history or a related field required by September 2027. The department seeks excellence in instruction, research, and service and seeks someone who will look forward to taking on administrative responsibilities at some point in their careers. Applicants must submit a cover letter; curriculum vitae; a syllabus; and three letters of recommendation, at least one of which should speak directly to the applicant’s teaching experience; and an example of the candidate’s scholarship.  Teaching evaluations would also be helpful for evaluating the candidate’s portfolio. For full consideration, please submit application materials by December 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled. General Compensation/Benefits Statement DePaul University has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as (but not limited to) the qualifications, education, experience, and training of the selected candidate, the scope and responsibilities of the position, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information. DePaul University offers excellent benefits, including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, and tuition benefit. Further information regarding benefits can be found here: https://offices.depaul.edu/human-resources/benefits/Pages/default.aspx . About DePaul University's Academic Calendar Except for the College of Law, DePaul University operates on a quarter system. Classes in Autumn, Winter, and Spring quarters are 11 weeks in length (including finals week) and Summer courses, in two sessions, are typically 5 weeks in length.  The College of Law operates on the semester system. Classes in the Fall and Spring semesters are 16 weeks in length (including finals week) and it offers a Summer Session of 7 weeks (including final exams)."
    },
    "https://ekze.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/2034": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Category: Office & Admin Support JobFunction: Executive and Admin Assistants JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Chicago, IL, United States The Executive Assistant serves as the primary administrative partner to the President and provides high-level operational support to the Office of the President. The role is responsible for managing the President's calendar, travel, expenses, and daily administrative activities. The position also provides calendar support to the Chief of Staff and works closely with the Deputy Chief of Staff to ensure effective execution of presidential priorities. The Highlights: The Executive Assistant serves as the primary administrative partner to the President and provides high-level operational support to the Office of the President. The role is responsible for managing the President's calendar, travel, expenses, and daily administrative activities. The position also provides calendar support to the Chief of Staff and works closely with the Deputy Chief of Staff to ensure effective execution of presidential priorities. What You'll Do: Calendar Management Manage and strategically prioritize the President's and Chief of Staff's calendars, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities and effective use of executive time. Coordinate all aspects of presidential scheduling and executive engagements, including meetings with trustees, donors, alumni, university leaders, elected officials, and external partners. Anticipate needs, resolve scheduling and logistical challenges, and ensure all meetings are supported with appropriate materials, participants, and preparation to facilitate successful outcomes. President's Office Administration Exercise discretion, sound judgment, and executive presence while serving as a key point of contact for trustees, university leaders, and external stakeholders. Manage executive document preparation, routing, approvals, and follow-up to ensure efficient and timely decision-making. Oversee daily office operations, maintain effective administrative systems and workflows, and proactively resolve operational issues. Coordinate University House scheduling and logistics in support of presidential and institutional priorities. Travel Management & Expense Administration Coordinate domestic and international travel, develop detailed itineraries and briefing materials, manage travel logistics, and proactively resolve issues to support successful presidential engagements. Oversee the preparation, submission, and reconciliation of presidential expenses, ensuring accuracy, timeliness, and compliance with university policies. Board & Office of the Secretary Support Coordinate logistics for Board of Trustees meetings, committee meetings, retreats, trustee events, and presidential engagements. Manage meeting and event operations, including scheduling, catering, technology, attendee coordination, and materials distribution. Support trustee visits and institutional events, ensuring a seamless experience for participants and stakeholders. What You'll Need: High school diploma, required. Bachelor’s degree, preferred. 5 or more years of experience supporting a senior executive, president, CEO, or equivalent leader. Demonstrated expertise in complex calendaring and executive travel management. Exceptional organizational, prioritization, and problem-solving skills. Strong written and verbal communication abilities. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Outlook, Microsoft Office Suite, and virtual collaboration tools. Ability to manage highly confidential information with discretion and professionalism. For consideration, please include a resume and cover letter. The anticipated hiring range for this position is: $27.57 to $35.71/hr. The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position. Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Perks: Working for a stable and well-known University. Top choice medical, dental, and vision benefits. Retirement plan matching contribution of 8%. Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Generous paid time off, sick time, holidays, floating holidays, and more! Full-Time Benefits Vincentian Mission: Guided by an ethic of Vincentian personalism and professionalism, DePaul compassionately upholds the dignity of all members of its diverse, multi-faith, and inclusive community. We seek to hire collaborative, open-minded, and dedicated professionals who are committed to advancing our university mission to making education accessible to all, with special attention to including underserved and underrepresented communities. Successful candidates thrive in an environment where ideas and perspectives representing a wide variety of cultures, backgrounds and experiences are welcome and supported. Required Background Check: Employment at DePaul University is contingent on passing a background check. Only final candidates who are extended an offer of employment will undergo a background check. DePaul University is an Equal Opportunity employer . All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, marital status, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, genetic information or any other legally protected status, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local EEO laws. "
    },
    "https://ekze.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/2028": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Category: Advancement JobFunction: Alumni Relations JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Chicago, IL, United States The Assistant Director supports the development and implementation of alumni programs and services that foster meaningful engagement, advance the university's strategic priorities, and build a lifelong pipeline of engagement from students to alumni. The Assistant Director is responsible for developing and managing initiatives that strengthen connections between students, alumni, and the university. The Highlights: The Assistant Director supports the development and implementation of alumni programs and services that foster meaningful engagement, advance the university's strategic priorities, and build a lifelong pipeline of engagement from students to alumni. The Assistant Director is responsible for developing and managing initiatives that strengthen connections between students, alumni, and the university. Key responsibilities include advising the Future Alumni Association student organization; overseeing the Young Alumni Committee and Legacy Program; partnering with campus departments to integrate alumni into student-facing programs and experiences; and managing DePaulConnect, the university's online networking platform for students and alumni. The Assistant Director also identifies and develops opportunities that encourage lifelong alumni engagement through mentorship, volunteerism, networking, and programming. As a member of the Alumni Relations team, the Assistant Director remains informed about new and ongoing university initiatives and actively identifies opportunities to collaborate across campus, leveraging partnerships and programs to enhance alumni engagement. What You'll Do: 1. DePaul Connect Management: Serve as the primary administrator for DePaulConnect, the university's online networking platform, ensuring the effective use of its features to maximize student and alumni engagement. Manage platform operations, including user support, group administration, Flash Mentoring opportunities, data integrity, troubleshooting, and ongoing optimization. Promote adoption of the platform through strategic outreach and collaboration with campus partners while identifying opportunities to expand engagement and enhance the user experience. 2. Relationship Management: Build and maintain strong partnerships with campus departments and key stakeholders, serving as the primary Alumni Relations contact for assigned initiatives. Cultivate relationships with students, alumni, and volunteers who have an affinity for specific student organizations, programs, or shared experiences, connecting them with meaningful engagement, mentorship, volunteer, networking, and philanthropic opportunities that strengthen lifelong connections to the university. 3. Event and Program Management: Coordinate and support alumni-focused events, programs, and initiatives that engage students, young alumni, alumni volunteers, and targeted alumni audiences. Responsibilities include planning, promotion, logistics, volunteer coordination, on-site event support, and post-event assessment and data collection to inform future programming. 4. Planning: Collaborate with the Senior Director of Alumni Relations and Alumni Relations colleagues to develop strategic goals, priorities, and engagement plans that align with Advancement objectives and support a lifelong alumni engagement pipeline from student to alumni. • Responsible for monitoring income and expenses related to alumni programming. What You'll Need: • Bachelor's degree required with emphasis in communication, marketing or related field. • Minimum 2- 3 years experience. • Strong interpersonal and communication skills. • Able to manage several projects simultaneously and work effectively under time constraints. • Build effective, open, and communicative relationships with internal and external constituents. • Self-motivated and adaptable to a variety of tasks. • Computer literacy, database management skills. • Broad understanding of higher-education issues and knowledge of volunteer-focused environments. The anticipated hiring range for this position is: $47,783 to $55,000. The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position. Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Perks: Working for a stable and well-known University. Top choice medical, dental, and vision benefits. Retirement plan matching contribution of 8%. Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Generous paid time off, sick time, holidays, floating holidays, and more! Full-Time Benefits For consideration, please include a resume and cover letter. Vincentian Mission: Guided by an ethic of Vincentian personalism and professionalism, DePaul compassionately upholds the dignity of all members of its diverse, multi-faith, and inclusive community. We seek to hire collaborative, open-minded, and dedicated professionals who are committed to advancing our university mission to making education accessible to all, with special attention to including underserved and underrepresented communities. Successful candidates thrive in an environment where ideas and perspectives representing a wide variety of cultures, backgrounds and experiences are welcome and supported. Required Background Check: Employment at DePaul University is contingent on passing a background check. Only final candidates who are extended an offer of employment will undergo a background check. DePaul University is an Equal Opportunity employer . All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, marital status, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, genetic information or any other legally protected status, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local EEO laws. "
    },
    "https://ekze.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/2041": {
      "title": "Degree Conferral Coordinator",
      "description": "Category: Office & Admin Support JobFunction: Admin Manager/Supervisor JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Chicago, IL, United States The Degree Conferral Coordinator is responsible for providing technical and functional support for the University’s Degree Progress Report (DPR), Degree Conferral, and other academic applications maintained by the Office of the University Registrar (UR). This position will encode degree requirements within the DPR to be used for degree planning, academic advising and conferring degrees. The Highlights: The Degree Conferral Coordinator is responsible for providing technical and functional support for the University’s Degree Progress Report (DPR), Degree Conferral, and other academic applications maintained by the Office of the University Registrar (UR). This position will encode degree requirements within the DPR to be used for degree planning, academic advising and conferring degrees. This position will also coordinate updates with the college offices and programs, conduct final audits of student records to determine eligibility, and award degrees. The Coordinator will also deliver accurate degree progress reports to student population, faculty, and staff and must maintain a broad knowledge of DePaul graduation requirements. The Coordinator works with academic units to deliver unofficial copies of the curriculum encoded within reports and ensures information is accurate and accessible tool for the university community. This position ensures that University academic policies and procedures, and best practices in records maintenance, are observed and that all functions are performed according to institutional standards, and federal rules and regulations. What You'll Do: 1. Analyze and perform programing (encoding) to translate major, college and university requirements into a complex system that integrates course catalog, test credit, transferred coursework, and curriculum requirements to deliver accurate representation of the student’s academic progress toward completion of a degree. 2. Participate in the University’s Degree Conferral process. Protect the integrity of the DePaul degree by ensuring students who have applied for graduation have met the University and degree requirements by conducting the final audit before the degree is posted to the academic record. Identify process exemptions, follow protocol to secure appropriate academic officer sign-off, and documents transactions accordingly. 3. Collaborate in the development and regular maintenance (and ongoing coding of new specifications) of a number of delivered and customized PeopleSoft applications, which are essential for compliance with federal laws (like the OBBB). Support students, academic units and the Office of the University Registrar. Maintain various support applications, which include, the Online Declaration Tool, Advisor Assignments, Advising Notes, Degree Conferral/Graduation application, dynamic transfer guides. Create and apply academic milestones, course mapping features, and update student program plan/stacks. 4. Conduct regular audits to ensure data integrity across multiple applications within purview. Perform thorough PeopleSoft patch cycle testing to identify all potential problems and works with UR's Systems team to address problem before the patch is applied to Production. What You'll Need: • Bachelor’s degree, required. • Minimum 3-5 years of experience in higher education, particularly in Student Records or Academic Advising; or in a position with exposure to data structure, experience interpreting and enacting policy, or history of working with partners and holding them accountable. • Knowledge of, or willingness to learn PeopleSoft Campus Solutions, in particular the Academic Advisement module, Student Retention/Advising software, and Microsoft Office suite. • Basic understanding of and knowledge of University resources for students. • Strong understanding of database principles and experience with troubleshooting. • Ability to administer Student Records and Advising functions with accuracy and awareness of policy. • Ability to work positively in a demanding, high volume, fast-paced environment. • Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. • Ability to negotiate diplomatically. • Ability to handle multiple projects simultaneously. • Excellent written and oral communication skills. The anticipated hiring range for this position is: $47,783 to $55,000. The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position. Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Perks: Working for a stable and well-known University. Top choice medical, dental, and vision benefits. Retirement plan matching contribution of 8%. Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Generous paid time off, sick time, holidays, floating holidays, and more! Full-Time Benefits For consideration, please include a resume and cover letter. Vincentian Mission: Guided by an ethic of Vincentian personalism and professionalism, DePaul compassionately upholds the dignity of all members of its diverse, multi-faith, and inclusive community. We seek to hire collaborative, open-minded, and dedicated professionals who are committed to advancing our university mission to making education accessible to all, with special attention to including underserved and underrepresented communities. Successful candidates thrive in an environment where ideas and perspectives representing a wide variety of cultures, backgrounds and experiences are welcome and supported. Required Background Check: Employment at DePaul University is contingent on passing a background check. Only final candidates who are extended an offer of employment will undergo a background check. DePaul University is an Equal Opportunity employer . All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, marital status, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, genetic information or any other legally protected status, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local EEO laws. "
    },
    "https://ekze.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/2043": {
      "title": "Assistant Director,  Academic Advising",
      "description": "Category: Academic Support JobFunction: Advising JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Chicago, IL, United States The Assistant Director is a member of Office of Advising and Student Services (OASS) advising team and works collaboratively with the psychology department. They share the psychology advising caseload with two other staff academic advisors in College of Science and Health and works collaboratively with the CSH pre-health advising team. The Assistant Director directly report to the Director of advising services in the OASS. The Highlights: The Assistant Director is a member of Office of Advising and Student Services (OASS) advising team and works collaboratively with the psychology department. They share the psychology advising caseload with two other staff academic advisors in College of Science and Health and works collaboratively with the CSH pre-health advising team. The Assistant Director directly report to the Director of advising services in the OASS. What You'll Do: 1. Provide holistic academic advising for new and continuing undergraduate students majoring and minoring in psychology by conducting individual advising appointments and/or hosting group advising sessions. Advising includes, but is not limited to academic schedules, long term course planning and class sequencing, progress toward graduation, academic success, career aspirations, basic financial aid options and navigating the SAP appeal process and initiating referrals to appropriate resources. Logs advising summaries and advising notes into OneDePaul. Coordinates scheduling of advising appointments via OneDePaul. Advises students on interpreting university policies and procedures, specifically academic policies and procedures. Monitors students in good academic standing or on academic probation. Supports CSH retention and persistence efforts by meeting with students on academic probation. Supports CSH degree conferral auditing efforts through graduation advising appointments. 2. Supports new student academic advising during Premiere and Transition DePaul orientation, including mid-year orientation and ad hoc academic advising during the start of each term. Assists with presentations on behalf of an academic department or college to current, prospective, and new students and guests during orientation and/or Admission events. Assists with Premiere and Transition DePaul orientation file preparation, session monitoring, and attendance check-in. 3. Liaises with the Department of Psychology department leadership and faculty and staff. Updates and maintains faculty and staff advisor assignments and assists with sending regular advising communication to students, staff, and faculty. Assists with updating the psychology advising materials. Participates regularly in OASS meetings and events and psychology department meeting when matters of advising and curriculum are discussed. Attends the annual Psych Night. What You'll Need: -Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree in Student/Personnel Counseling, Higher Education, and/or related field preferred. -Three to five years of experience based on type of experience and education. -Excellent verbal and written communication skills. -Strong analytical skills and detail oriented. -Strong organizational skills. -Ability to work independently and as part of a group. -Ability to work with a diverse population of students, faculty and staff. -Ability to plan, prioritize and meet deadlines. The anticipated hiring range for this position is: $47,783 to $59,059. The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position. Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Perks: Working for a stable and well-known University. Top choice medical, dental, and vision benefits. Retirement plan matching contribution of 8%. Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Generous paid time off, sick time, holidays, floating holidays, and more! Full-Time Benefits For consideration, please include a resume and cover letter. Vincentian Mission: Guided by an ethic of Vincentian personalism and professionalism, DePaul compassionately upholds the dignity of all members of its diverse, multi-faith, and inclusive community. We seek to hire collaborative, open-minded, and dedicated professionals who are committed to advancing our university mission to making education accessible to all, with special attention to including underserved and underrepresented communities. Successful candidates thrive in an environment where ideas and perspectives representing a wide variety of cultures, backgrounds and experiences are welcome and supported. Required Background Check: Employment at DePaul University is contingent on passing a background check. Only final candidates who are extended an offer of employment will undergo a background check. DePaul University is an Equal Opportunity employer . All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, marital status, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, genetic information or any other legally protected status, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local EEO laws. "
    },
    "https://ekze.fa.us2.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1001/job/2047": {
      "title": "Office Manager & Clinical Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Category: Finance and Accounting JobFunction: Financial/Acctg Clerical JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Chicago, IL, United States The Clinical Services Coordinator oversees and coordinates the Family &Community Services operations, which include patient intake, appointments, behavioral healthcare billing, invoicing and patient payments, claims submission, continuing education processing, grant proposal coordination, as well as the overall responsibility for the Electronic Medical Record System. The Highlights: The Clinical Services Coordinator oversees and coordinates the Family &Community Services operations, which include patient intake, appointments, behavioral healthcare billing, invoicing and patient payments, claims submission, continuing education processing, grant proposal coordination, as well as the overall responsibility for the Electronic Medical Record System. The Clinical Services Coordinator works directly with patients as well as insurance and healthcare providers to coordinate patient care from referral to discharge as well as monitor the processes to get all claims processed, appealed, and paid. Manages clinician and facility credentialing with insurance companies and payers. This position may also serves as a back-up receptionist and support of the front office functions of DePaul Family & Community Services as needed. What You'll Do: 1. Clinical Care Coordination. Responsible for clinical case documentation, opening and closing cases and reviewing all clinical documentation to ensure everything is needed in order to bill for cases. Responsible for preparing fee for service billing for local school-based grant projects. Responsible for managing utilization review internal auditing. Responsible for consumer satisfaction survey processes and follow up interviews. Responsible for conducting billing audits as part of required accreditation and certification requirements. 2. Software Management/Maintenance. Oversees and manage the Electronic Medical Record system. Responsible for system upkeep and maintenance, working with external parties as needed. Manages system users, upgrades, etc. 3. Claims and Billing. Responsible for all of center's billings/claims. Works directly with the insurance companies, healthcare providers, and patients to get claims processed and paid including verifying patients' insurance coverage, answering billing questions, and coordinating invoicing on unpaid accounts. Responsible for maintaining all medical records, overseeing the student workers functioning in Office Assistant role. 4. Office Management. Responsible for overseeing general office operations for Family Community Services including facility access management, work orders, supplies ordering, student hiring, and front desk staffing. Response for ensuring proper processes for patient intake, tracking, etc. Serves as main support person for the Center's Director in assisting with tracking of clinical hours, fee for service work, grant proposals, medical/grant billings and appointments, etc. Supervisory Duties: Manages front office student workers, front office coverage and delegation of administrative tasks. What You'll Need: • Bachelor’s degree, Master's, preferred. • 3 years previous office management, healthcare billing, and electronic medical records experience in a medical, behavioral health or social services setting. • Must be able to work some evening hours and maintain a flexible schedule. • Must be able to work independently and meet deadlines. • Must be able to work in a team environment and provide excellent customer service to all stakeholders (clients, staff, faculty, and the community). • Advanced computer skills required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. • Proficiency in producing data and narrative reports for a professional audience. • Excellent organizational and communication skills required. • Must be reliable, organized, detail-oriented and capable of working with minimal supervision. • Should be comfortable interacting with children, adolescents, and families. The anticipated hiring range for this position is: $23.45 to $27.47/hr. The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position. Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Perks: Working for a stable and well-known University. Top choice medical, dental, and vision benefits. Retirement plan matching contribution of 8%. Tuition waivers for employees and dependents. Generous paid time off, sick time, holidays, floating holidays, and more! Full-Time Benefit s For consideration, please include a resume and cover letter. Vincentian Mission: Guided by an ethic of Vincentian personalism and professionalism, DePaul compassionately upholds the dignity of all members of its diverse, multi-faith, and inclusive community. We seek to hire collaborative, open-minded, and dedicated professionals who are committed to advancing our university mission to making education accessible to all, with special attention to including underserved and underrepresented communities. Successful candidates thrive in an environment where ideas and perspectives representing a wide variety of cultures, backgrounds and experiences are welcome and supported. Required Background Check: Employment at DePaul University is contingent on passing a background check. Only final candidates who are extended an offer of employment will undergo a background check. DePaul University is an Equal Opportunity employer . All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, marital status, physical or mental disability, protected veteran status, genetic information or any other legally protected status, in accordance with applicable federal, state and local EEO laws. "
    }
  },
